findings.evidence:
service.py:1369-1382 in full:

  def allowed_issuance_for_domain(common_name, extensions):
      check_permission_for_cn = True if common_name else False
      if extensions and extensions.get("sub_alt_names"):
          for san in extensions["sub_alt_names"]["names"]:
              if isinstance(san, x509.DNSName):
                  if san.value == common_name:
                      check_permission_for_cn = False
                  is_authorized_for_domain(san.value)
      if check_permission_for_cn:
          is_authorized_for_domain(common_name)

`is_authorized_for_domain` is called only under `isinstance(san, x509.DNSName)`. Any other subject-alternative-name type in the same list - x509.IPAddress, x509.UniformResourceIdentifier, x509.RFC822Name, x509.DirectoryName, x509.OtherName - falls through the loop with no authorization call, and does not set `check_permission_for_cn` either. The two guards that skip the function entirely are visible at the call site, views.py:538-539: it runs only when `not g.user.is_admin_or_global_cert_issuer and not data["authority"].is_private_authority`. A request that supplies an empty `common_name` and only non-DNSName SANs passes through the function with zero authorization calls made.
